## Task
Re-rebase all four TA 0.9 branches from their current `aa86a2a9` base onto the
**last compiling commit `55e24be9`** (#1469, the immediate parent of `aa86a2a9`).
`aa86a2a9` (#1334) does not compile — it reintroduced `interfaces.` refs in
`internal/engines/saturation/engine.go` after the `internal/interfaces`→`domain`
rename (#1449), so `go build`/`make test`/`make lint` cannot run on it. `55e24be9`
has the rename and no stray `interfaces.` refs → it builds. (Upstream fix is
already open as PR #1477 but not merged; we are not waiting on it.)

Do this one worktree at a time via `EnterWorktree`; verify `pwd` +
`git branch --show-current` after each switch and before any operation.

## Per branch — rebase mechanism
Each branch is currently based on `aa86a2a9` with our commits on top (and, for C,
the two reworded subjects). Move that same commit stack onto `55e24be9`:

```
git rebase --onto 55e24be9 aa86a2a9
```

This replays only our commits onto `55e24be9` (drops the broken `aa86a2a9` from
underneath — it was never our commit). Expected clean on all four: `#1334`'s only
change is `modeLabelForAnalyzer` in `engine.go`, a region none of the four branches
touch. C's reworded commit messages carry through unchanged. If any branch hits a
conflict, stop and write a `plan__*.md` handoff.

Confirm the new base after rebasing: `git merge-base HEAD upstream/main` and
`git log --oneline -1 $(git rev-list --max-parents=0 ... )` — simplest check:
`git log --oneline 55e24be9..HEAD` should show only our commits, and
`git rev-parse 55e24be9` should be `HEAD`'s ancestor with nothing from `aa86a2a9`.

## Full gates this time (55e24be9 compiles)
Run on every branch — these are now runnable:
- `make test`
- `gofmt -l ./internal/... ./pkg/... ./cmd/...` (must be empty)
- `make lint`
- `go build ./...`
- `-race` where relevant on `ta-veto-liveness` (`make test` with race, per its prior runs).
- DCO: `git log 55e24be9..HEAD --format="%b" | grep -c Signed-off-by` must equal the commit count.

## Do NOT push
Per coder rules, do not `git push` (these are force-pushes; Dean runs them).
When all four are rebased onto `55e24be9` and all gates are green, write a
`plan__*.md` handoff reporting, per branch: new tip SHA, base confirmed
`55e24be9`, and each gate's pass/fail. Dean force-pushes; PRs follow.
